  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Headline GPU-only maxima (-60% TTFT / -37% JCT on Qwen3-8B CC4) and two-tier maxima (-76% TTFT / -60% JCT on Qwen3-235B CC4 with 256K/256K tiers and 144K mean context) correspond to distinct models and capacity regimes and cannot be merged; on 128K/128K matched trace, 235B two-tier TTFT gain drops to -49%.",
    "Benefits require intermediate cache pressure: fitting sessions (8B N=2 at 99.5% hit; 4:1 CPU/GPU at 92-94% hit) leave <3% gain, severe 1:1 CPU starvation yields -10%, and external tool-wait dominance (FreeInference) shrinks JCT reduction to -2%.",
    "GPU-only capacities (256K/192K/384K) are explicitly capped to trigger eviction, CC initial prompts and FI block IDs use synthetic tokens matching trace lengths/sharing, and replay feeds recorded replies rather than sampled outputs (releasing generated KV after each turn).",
    "Cost model and block recomputation assume full causal attention in every layer and write-back single-node CPU tiering; sliding-window, hybrid linear/Mamba, KV-compressed MLA, and disaggregated PD setups are untested.",
    "Positional savings depend on cache-aware LPM scheduling (FCFS raises full private-history misses to 21.0-21.4% on 32B/235B and roughly halves TTFT gains), and no public Penelope code repository URL is included in arXiv:2611.00391v1."
  ],
